---

<BaseLayout
  title="How to Apply for a Wolverhampton Private Hire Licence"
  description="How to apply for a Wolverhampton private hire licence: eligibility, documents, the medical and DBS checks, the knowledge test, and what happens after."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <main class="md:flex md:justify-center">
    <article class="prose prose-lg max-w-[750px]">
      <h1>How to Apply for a Wolverhampton Private Hire Licence</h1>

      <p>
        This page explains <strong>how to apply for a Wolverhampton private
        hire licence</strong> (the PHV driver's licence, often called the
        "taxi badge") — who can apply, what you'll need, the training and
        test, and what happens after you pass. Everything is in plain
        English, in the order you'll actually do it.
      </p>

      <h2>Am I eligible?</h2>

      <p>Before you start, check you meet the basic requirements:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Be at least 21 years old</strong> and have held a full UK
          driving licence for at least 12 months.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Have the right to work in the UK.</strong>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Pass a Group 2 medical</strong> — the higher standard that
          applies to professional drivers.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Pass an enhanced DBS check</strong> (criminal record check).
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        If any of these might be an issue — for example points on your
        licence or a past conviction — check the council's official guidance
        before you spend money on the application, as decisions on individual
        cases rest with the council.
      </p>

      <h2>What documents do I need?</h2>

      <p>You'll need to gather:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Your <strong>full UK driving licence</strong> (copy)</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Proof of identity</strong> — passport or government-issued
          ID
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Proof of address</strong> — a recent utility bill or bank
          statement
        </li>
        <li>Your <strong>Group 2 medical certificate</strong></li>
        <li>Your <strong>enhanced DBS certificate</strong></li>
        <li>
          <strong>Proof of right to work</strong>, if applicable — passport,
          residence permit or visa
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Have originals or approved copies ready, and make sure names and
        addresses match across your documents — mismatches are a common
        cause of delays.
      </p>

      <h2>How does the application process work?</h2>

      <p>At a high level, the process runs in this order:</p>

      <ol>
        <li>Confirm you meet the eligibility requirements above.</li>
        <li>Gather your documents.</li>
        <li>Apply for your enhanced DBS check.</li>
        <li>
          Complete the Private Hire Driver Application Form, available from
          the Wolverhampton Council website.
        </li>
        <li>Pass the knowledge test.</li>
        <li>Attend an interview with a licensing officer, if required.</li>
        <li>Submit your application and pay the fee.</li>
        <li>Wait for processing — then your badge is issued.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>What training and testing is involved?</h2>

      <p>
        The knowledge test is taken alongside a short training course. The
        test itself is multiple-choice: <strong>28 questions</strong>, and to
        pass you must score at least <strong>21 out of 28</strong> (75%)
        <strong>and</strong> answer all <strong>8 key questions</strong>
        correctly — getting even one key question wrong is an automatic fail,
        whatever your overall score. Read our guides to
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/how-to-pass/"
          >passing the Wolverhampton PHV test</a
        >
        and
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/8-key-questions/"
          >the 8 key questions</a
        >
        before you book.
      </p>

      <p>
        Once you've booked your test, start practising early — the
        <a
          href="https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/phv-prep-uk-taxi-badge-test/id6776364932"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">PHV Prep UK app</a
        >
        has 300+ exam-style questions and timed mock exams scored exactly
        like the real test, so you know you're ready before test day.
      </p>

      <h2>How much does it cost?</h2>

      <p>
        Each attempt at the training course and test costs around
        <strong>£50</strong> (training course plus test). And the attempts are
        limited: only <strong>3 attempts</strong> are permitted. If you don't
        pass within these 3 attempts, your application is voided and you'll
        need to wait <strong>12 months</strong> before starting the
        application and training process again — see
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/if-you-fail/"
          >what happens if you fail the Wolverhampton PHV test</a
        >
        for the full picture.
      </p>

      <p>
        The course and test cost is separate from the council's own licence
        and application fee, the DBS check fee, and the cost of your medical.
        Those amounts vary, so check the current rates directly on the
        Wolverhampton Council website before you budget — and remember
        you're budgeting for the whole process, not just the test.
      </p>

      <h2>What happens after I pass?</h2>

      <p>
        Passing the knowledge test is one part of the application, not the
        end of it. Once your medical, DBS check, documents and test are all
        complete and approved by the council, your private hire driver's
        licence can be issued. From then on, remember the basics of staying
        licensed: wear your badge on the upper part of your body, clearly
        visible, whenever you're working, and only carry passengers whose
        journeys are pre-booked through a licensed operator.
      </p>

      <h2>Renewing Your Wolverhampton PHV Driver Licence</h2>

      <p>
        Renewal is not automatic. You are responsible for submitting your
        application on time — missing the deadline means you cannot legally
        operate Wolverhampton-licensed vehicles.
      </p>

      <h3>Timeline</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>8–12 weeks before expiry</strong> — start gathering your
          documents.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>4–8 weeks before expiry</strong> — the council will email
          your personal renewal reference number.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>At least 10 working days before expiry</strong> — submit
          your completed application. Do not leave this until the last
          moment.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>If you haven't received your renewal email 4 weeks before
          expiry</strong> — contact the licensing team directly. Include your
          full name and current badge number:
          <a href="mailto:driver.lic@wolverhampton.gov.uk"
            >driver.lic@wolverhampton.gov.uk</a
          >
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Grace period</h3>

      <p>
        If your licence has recently lapsed, the council allows up to
        <strong>28 days post-expiry</strong> to treat the application as a
        late renewal rather than a brand-new application. Do not rely on
        this. Submit before your expiry date.
      </p>

      <h3>Documents required</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>In-date DBS certificate</strong> — must be no older than 12
          months from the date of your former licence expiry. Basic,
          standard, or enhanced are all accepted, as is registration on the
          DBS Update Service.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Completed medical form</strong> — required every 5 years
          for drivers aged 45 and over, and every year for drivers aged 65
          and over.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Proof of insurance.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>V5 vehicle document</strong> (if applicable).</li>
        <li><strong>HMRC Tax Check code.</strong></li>
        <li>
          <strong>Certificate of Good Character</strong> — required if you
          have lived or worked outside the UK for 3 or more continuous months
          since age 18.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>How to submit</h3>

      <p>
        Use the
        <a
          href="https://iapply.co.uk/taxilicensing/renewDriverReference"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">iApply Driver Renewal Portal</a
        >.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Limited Company applicants:</strong> all Directors must
        submit a DBS certificate.
      </p>

      <p>Post original DBS certificates to:</p>

      <p>
        Taxi Licensing<br />
        City of Wolverhampton Council<br />
        Civic Centre, St. Peter's Square<br />
        Wolverhampton WV1 1SH
      </p>

      <h2>Where to go next</h2>

      <p>
        The application is the paperwork — the test is the hurdle. Start with
        our full guide on
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/how-to-pass/"
          >how to pass the Wolverhampton PHV test</a
        >, make sure you understand
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/8-key-questions/"
          >the 8 key questions</a
        >, and try some free
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/practice-questions/"
          >practice questions and answers</a
        >. You can also learn more about the app on the
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk">PHV Prep UK page</a>, get help via
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/support">support</a>, or read our
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>PHV Prep UK is an independent study aid.</strong> It is not
        affiliated with, authorised by, or endorsed by City of Wolverhampton
        Council or any licensing authority. Always check the council's
        official guidance for the latest application requirements and fees.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
